{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123219","id":4449497833,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCTXy6Q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123219","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123219.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123219.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123219","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123219/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123219/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123219/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/24d25e6f4dd5b77d253afe31deba15dfd9659c60","number":123219,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Add a manual reference-cycle collector for RefCounted","user":{"login":"NAVEENKUMARKR777","id":165763161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCeFYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165763161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777","html_url":"https://github.com/NAVEENKUMARKR777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #7038\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`RefCounted` is backed by a bare atomic reference count with no cycle\r\ndetection (`core/object/ref_counted.h`). A reference cycle — for example two\r\nGDScript objects that hold a reference to each other, with nothing external\r\nreferencing either — never reaches zero on its own and leaks for the\r\nlifetime of the process. The only existing guidance (documented on\r\n`RefCounted` itself) is to manually break such cycles with `weakref()`.\r\n\r\n**What this adds**: a `CycleCollector` (`core/object/cycle_collector.h/.cpp`)\r\nimplementing Bacon & Rajan's synchronous trial-deletion algorithm — the same\r\none used by CPython's `gc` module:\r\n\r\n- On every `RefCounted::unreference()` that decrements without reaching\r\n  zero, the object is buffered as a possible cycle root.\r\n- The new `Engine.collect_cycles()` walks the buffered set, trial-decrementing\r\n  a *local scratch* refcount (never the real atomic) along every reachable\r\n  edge, and identifies as garbage anything left with a scratch count of zero\r\n  — i.e. objects proven reachable only from within the traversed subgraph.\r\n- Edges are only followed through a script instance's members (two new\r\n  `ScriptInstance` virtuals — `get_gc_member_count()`/`get_gc_member()` —\r\n  implemented by `GDScriptInstance`) and through `Array`/`Dictionary`\r\n  contents, never through arbitrary exposed properties or getters, which\r\n  would be unsafe to re-enter mid-collection.\r\n\r\n**A correctness subtlety worth flagging for review**: freeing a proven cycle\r\nisn't as simple as calling `memdelete()` on each member in turn — they still\r\nhold live references *to each other*, so destroying one the ordinary way can\r\nfree another member as a side effect, which the collector would then try to\r\nfree again itself (double free). This is handled by padding each garbage\r\nobject's real refcount by one, severing every outgoing edge through the\r\nordinary safe `Variant`-release path (a third new virtual,\r\n`clear_gc_member()`, which can't prematurely reach zero thanks to the\r\npadding), then removing the padding with a real `unreference()` — by then\r\nevery edge within the cycle has already been severed, so this is provably\r\nthe last reference and freeing it is safe.\r\n\r\n**Deliberate scope limits** (this is already a fairly large change; I tried\r\nto keep it to something that could plausibly be reviewed and merged rather\r\nthan a full engine-wide GC rewrite):\r\n- Collection is **manual only** — `Engine.collect_cycles()` must be called\r\n  explicitly; nothing calls it automatically every frame. Whether/how to\r\n  wire up automatic periodic collection seems like a separate design\r\n  discussion (frequency, thread-safety implications, performance cost of\r\n  scanning every frame vs. staleness of leaked memory).\r\n- Must be called from the main thread. It doesn't attempt concurrent or\r\n  incremental collection.\r\n- Only cycles routed through GDScript members and/or `Array`/`Dictionary`\r\n  contents are detected. A `RefCounted` with no script instance (e.g. a\r\n  plain `Resource`) can't be the source of a detected cycle.\r\n\r\nGiven the size of this change and that #7038 has had no prior fix attempts\r\nin ~9 years, I'd welcome input from core devs on whether this scope and API\r\nshape (`Engine.collect_cycles()`) make sense before going further (e.g.\r\nautomatic collection, exposing it to C#/GDExtension script instances, etc.)\r\n— happy to discuss on Contributors Chat if useful.\r\n\r\n**Testing**: added `tests/core/object/test_cycle_collector.cpp` (3 cases: a\r\ndirect two-object cycle, a cycle routed through an `Array`, and a\r\nfalse-positive check for an object referenced twice that isn't part of any\r\ncycle — all passing). Also verified against the full existing test suite\r\n(1423/1423 cases, 422,857/422,857 assertions, no regressions) and manually\r\nagainst a real GDScript scene reproducing the original leak end-to-end.\r\n\r\n**AI disclosure**: This change (algorithm design, implementation, and\r\ntesting) was developed with Claude (Anthropic), directed and reviewed by\r\nme. During development, Claude's first draft of the finalization step\r\ncalled `memdelete()` directly on cycle members, which it then identified\r\nitself as unsafe (the double-free hazard described above) and corrected to\r\nthe pad/sever/release sequence before I asked for this to be verified by an\r\nactual build and test run. I read and understand the diff before submitting\r\nit.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T07:57:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T22:32:18Z","closed_at":"2026-09-05T10:37:00Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"fb713b4d3cd3c3c457674dc4726997414e7daf24","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"NAVEENKUMARKR777:feature/gdscript-cycle-collector","ref":"feature/gdscript-cycle-collector","repo":{"id":1357859302,"node_id":"R_kgDOUO9J5g","name":"godot","full_name":"NAVEENKUMARKR777/godot","owner":{"login":"NAVEENKUMARKR777","id":165763161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCeFYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165763161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777","html_url":"https://github.com/NAVEENKUMARKR777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs